<article class="env-definition" id="06FS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06FS">Definition <span data-tag="06FS">101.17.1</span>.</a> Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a morphism of algebraic stacks. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $f$ <em>locally of finite type</em> if the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/06FM" data-tag="06FM">101.16.1</a> hold with $\mathcal{P} = \text{locally of finite type}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>of finite type</em> if it is locally of finite type and quasi-compact. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>